1942 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Modifier System Fails Users \050Critical\051\n\nThe drink customization system was the most consistent source of task failure across all 15 sessions\056 Participants could not find modifiers\054 did not recognize the underline as a tappable element\054 and were confused by quantity controls \050especially selecting \042none\042 for an ingredient\051\056 When modifiers were found\054 the tap interaction frequently did not register or produced unexpected results\056 One participant spent 2\0565 minutes searching before giving up\056 Another said\072 \042It makes me feel like a dummy\056\042\n\nThe downstream effect\072 participants abandoned modifiers and typed their customizations into the special instructions field instead\056 This workaround then collided with an undisclosed character limit that forced users to truncate their requests\056 The character count was not visible to users\054 and at least 7 of 15 participants hit this wall\056\n\nRecommendations Obscure the Menu \050High\051\n\nThe recommended drinks section dominates the screen on first load\054 and multiple participants mistook it for the full menu\056 Users scrolled through recommendations repeatedly without realizing the actual menu existed elsewhere\056 Tarun\047s first participant took 5 minutes to locate the menu\056 His third participant spent 2\0553 minutes scrolling back and forth\056 Observations from the sessions suggest that the Home and Menu navigation should be more visually prominent\054 the cards could be smaller\054 and that the Rewards and Account sections consume too much screen real estate relative to the core ordering function\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 1943 0 R
     /Pg 1040 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1943 0 obj
  << /K [ 1942 0 R ]
     /P 1948 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1040 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1944 0 obj
  << /ActualText (No Ingredients or Allergen Information \050Critical\051\n\nParticipants across multiple sessions noted the absence of ingredient lists and allergen information\056 The flavor descriptors used by Philz \050e\056g\056\054 \042creamy\054\042 \042sweet\042\051 were called \042non\055standard\042 and unintuitive\056 \n\nWhile the ingredient emblems were present\054 only one participant out of 15 actually found them\056 \n\nFor a food and beverage ordering app\054 this gap affects both the user experience and the company\047s potential liability exposure\056 At least 5 participants explicitly noted this absence\056 )
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 1945 0 R
     /Pg 1040 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

