1957 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Scrolling Behavior Traps Users in Recommendations\n\nThe app\047s default view surfaces a recommendations section that responds to standard vertical scroll and swipe gestures\054 but does not lead users to the main menu\056 Participants\047 natural scrolling behavior kept them cycling through recommended items\054 unaware that the full menu existed in a different section of the app\056 \n\nMultiple participants were observed spending significant time scrolling through recommendations before discovering the menu\054 with some requiring facilitator intervention to move forward\056 The gesture works mechanically\054 but the information architecture means that a user\047s most instinctive mobile interaction\054 scrolling down to see more\054 actively delays them from reaching the core ordering functionality\056\n\nDesire to Use\n\nParticipant sentiment was mixed\056 One participant rated the app a 10\054 another called it \042childish\054\042 and a third explicitly asked \042Is there a search bar\077\042 suggesting the app was missing functionality they expected\056 One younger participant found the experience \042very intuitive\042 and finished in 5\07239 total\054 which suggests the design can work once a user has learned the interaction patterns\056 However\054 the learning curve is steep enough that multiple first\055time users expressed frustration and confusion during initial use\056 The overall UI was described as \042clean\042 but \042less intuitive\042 than expected\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 1958 0 R
     /Pg 1522 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1958 0 obj
  << /K [ 1957 0 R ]
     /P 1963 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1522 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1959 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Modifier Tap Targets Don\047t Communicate Interactivity\n\nThe modifier controls rely on an underline visual convention to signal \042tappable\054\042 but participants did not recognize this as an interactive element\056 The affordance failed across age groups and platform familiarity levels\054 but usability issues skewed towards older people\056 \n\nTarun\047s second participant \042tried multiple times\042 with the tap motion and \042action did not register\056\042 Users\047 natural tap behavior yielded null results\054 leading them to assume the controls were display\055only rather than interactive\056 \n\nOne facilitator noted this was especially problematic for older participants\056\n\nKeyboard Obscures Text Input\n\nWhen participants tapped into the special instructions field\054 the mobile keyboard covered the text entry area\056 Nik\047s participant \042can\047t see word typing due to soft keyboard\056\042 The app does not scroll or reposition the input field above the keyboard\054 which is a standard mobile pattern that is missing here\056 \n\nWhile partly an OS\055level concern\054 the app is responsible for compensating\056)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 1960 0 R
     /Pg 1522 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

